<article class="env-lemma" id="01QS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01QS">Lemma <span data-tag="01QS">29.2.5</span>.</a> A composition of closed immersions is a closed immersion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have seen this in Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/02V0" data-tag="02V0">26.24.3</a>, but here is another proof. Namely, it follows from the characterization (3) of closed immersions in Lemma <a href="/tag/01QO" data-tag="01QO">29.2.1</a>. Since if $I \subset R$ is an ideal, and $\overline{J} \subset R/I$ is an ideal, then $\overline{J} = J/I$ for some ideal $J \subset R$ which contains $I$ and $(R/I)/\overline{J} = R/J$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>